From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryson <10244083+brysonwf@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:53:36 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: codecs: wcd934x: no headset detection on boards without
 a jack

Add the boolean DT property qcom,no-headset-jack. When it is set the codec does not set up MBHC, so set_jack returns
-ENOTSUPP (which the sdm845 machine driver already accepts). The Surface Duo has no headphone jack: MBHC measured the
floating HPH/MIC pins at every boot ("Impedance detect ramp error", "MONO plug type detected") and reported a phantom
headset (Headphone Jack + Headset Mic Jack controls on). The Duo's audio DT sets the property.

This patch was written by Claude (Anthropic's AI assistant) under the direction of Bryson, who reviewed and
tested it on a Surface Duo.

Signed-off-by: Bryson <10244083+brysonwf@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../bindings/sound/qcom,wcd934x.yaml           |  4 ++++
 .../sm8150-microsoft-surface-duo-audio.dtsi    |  4 ++++
 sound/soc/codecs/wcd934x.c                     | 18 ++++++++++++++----
 3 files changed, 22 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/qcom,wcd934x.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/qcom,wcd934x.yaml
index 3a7334e41..cb64266cd 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/qcom,wcd934x.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/qcom,wcd934x.yaml
@@ -79,6 +79,10 @@ properties:
     minimum: 1800000
     maximum: 2850000
 
+  qcom,no-headset-jack:
+    description: The board has no headset jack; the codec's headset detection (MBHC) is not set up
+    type: boolean
+
   qcom,hphl-jack-type-normally-closed:
     description: Indicates that HPHL jack switch type is normally closed
     type: boolean
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-microsoft-surface-duo-audio.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-microsoft-surface-duo-audio.dtsi
index 1a1ea787c..b57f514cc 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-microsoft-surface-duo-audio.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-microsoft-surface-duo-audio.dtsi
@@ -161,6 +161,10 @@ wcd9340: codec@1,0 {
 				qcom,micbias3-microvolt = <1800000>;
 				qcom,micbias4-microvolt = <1800000>;
 
+				/* The Duo has no headphone jack: without this the codec's headset detection measures the floating
+				 * HPH/MIC pins and reports a phantom mono headset ("Headphone Jack" + "Headset Mic Jack" = on) */
+				qcom,no-headset-jack;
+
 				#address-cells = <1>;
 				#size-cells = <1>;
 
diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd934x.c b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd934x.c
index c8db33f78..59f1bf1b3 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd934x.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd934x.c
@@ -549,6 +549,7 @@ struct wcd934x_codec {
 	/* mbhc module */
 	struct wcd_mbhc *mbhc;
 	struct wcd_mbhc_config mbhc_cfg;
+	bool no_headset_jack;
 	struct wcd_mbhc_intr intr_ids;
 	bool mbhc_started;
 	struct mutex micb_lock;
@@ -2172,9 +2173,11 @@ static int wcd934x_init_dmic(struct snd_soc_component *comp)
 	u32 def_dmic_rate, dmic_clk_drv;
 	int ret;
 
-	ret = wcd_dt_parse_mbhc_data(comp->dev, &wcd->mbhc_cfg);
-	if (ret)
-		return ret;
+	if (!wcd->no_headset_jack) {
+		ret = wcd_dt_parse_mbhc_data(comp->dev, &wcd->mbhc_cfg);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+	}
 
 	snd_soc_component_update_bits(comp, WCD934X_ANA_MICB1,
 				      WCD934X_MICB_VAL_MASK, wcd->common.micb_vout[0]);
@@ -3019,6 +3022,10 @@ static int wcd934x_comp_probe(struct snd_soc_component *component)
 		return ret;
 	}
 
+	/* boards without a headset jack: no headset detection (it reports a phantom headset on floating pins) */
+	if (wcd->no_headset_jack)
+		return 0;
+
 	if (wcd934x_mbhc_init(component))
 		dev_err(component->dev, "Failed to Initialize MBHC\n");
 
@@ -5829,6 +5836,8 @@ static int wcd934x_codec_parse_data(struct wcd934x_codec *wcd)
 
 	of_property_read_u32(dev->parent->of_node, "qcom,dmic-sample-rate",
 			     &wcd->dmic_sample_rate);
+	/* dev is the SLIMbus device: its own node is the codec node (dev->parent = the SLIMbus controller) */
+	wcd->no_headset_jack = of_property_read_bool(dev->of_node, "qcom,no-headset-jack");
 
 	cfg->mbhc_micbias = MIC_BIAS_2;
 	cfg->anc_micbias = MIC_BIAS_2;
@@ -5839,7 +5848,8 @@ static int wcd934x_codec_parse_data(struct wcd934x_codec *wcd)
 	cfg->hs_thr = 1700;
 	cfg->hph_thr = 50;
 
-	wcd_dt_parse_mbhc_data(dev, cfg);
+	if (!wcd->no_headset_jack)
+		wcd_dt_parse_mbhc_data(dev, cfg);
 
 	return 0;
 }
